 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
+<a id="req-vet-003"></a>
+
+Staff also ask the inverse question: which veterinarians hold a given specialty. A specialty directory answers it, listing every specialty the clinic knows by its stored name, each with the veterinarians holding it `[REQ-VET-003]`. Each veterinarian appears by full name, first name then last name. Every specialty appears on one page. The page lists specialties, not the full roster, so a veterinarian holding no specialty appears nowhere on it. The page is reached by its address alone; no other page links to it.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every specialty is listed by its stored name on a single page.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty held by veterinarians, when the specialty directory is opened, then each holder is listed under it by first name then last name.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the specialty directory is opened, then that veterinarian appears nowhere on it.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A specialty that no veterinarian holds is still listed, with no veterinarian under it.
+2. A veterinarian holding several specialties appears under each one.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
